                <details class="chart-data">
                  <summary>Read language-signal data</summary>
                  <div id="language-matrix-data" class="chart-data-list"></div>
                </details>
              </figure>

              <figure class="atlas-figure repeat-landscape-figure">
                <figcaption>
                  <span><b>04</b><strong>Repeat landscape</strong></span>
                  <small>Frequency × time span · exact and semantic groups</small>
                </figcaption>
                <div
                  id="repeat-landscape"
                  class="atlas-plot repeat-landscape"
                  aria-label="Repeated question groups by frequency and time span"
                ></div>
                <details class="chart-data">
                  <summary>Read repeat data</summary>
                  <div id="repeat-landscape-data" class="chart-data-list"></div>
                </details>
              </figure>

              <figure class="atlas-figure topic-momentum-figure">
                <figcaption>
                  <span><b>05</b><strong>Topic momentum</strong></span>
                  <small>Fading ← local movement → emerging</small>
                </figcaption>
                <div id="topic-momentum-state" class="atlas-forming">
                  <span></span>
                  <strong>Topic movement is still forming.</strong>
                  <small>The deterministic views are already usable.</small>
                </div>
                <div
                  id="topic-momentum"
                  class="atlas-plot topic-momentum is-hidden"
                  aria-label="Semantic topics by momentum and conversation count"
                ></div>
                <details class="chart-data">
                  <summary>Read topic-momentum data</summary>
                  <div id="topic-momentum-data" class="chart-data-list"></div>
                </details>
              </figure>

              <figure class="atlas-figure conversation-shape-figure">
                <figcaption>
                  <span><b>06</b><strong>Conversation shape</strong></span>
                  <small>Depth, weekday rhythm, and model mix · all history</small>
                </figcaption>
                <div
                  id="conversation-shape"
                  class="conversation-shape"
                  aria-label="Conversation depth, weekday rhythm, and model usage"
                ></div>
                <details class="chart-data">
                  <summary>Read conversation-shape data</summary>
                  <div id="conversation-shape-data" class="chart-data-list"></div>
                </details>
              </figure>

              <figure class="atlas-figure historical-shifts-figure">
                <figcaption>
                  <span><b>07</b><strong>What changed</strong></span>
                  <small id="historical-shifts-period">
                    All history · earlier third vs recent third · no model needed
                  </small>
                </figcaption>
                <div id="historical-shifts-state" class="atlas-forming">
                  <span></span>
                  <strong>Not enough months to compare yet.</strong>
                  <small>Three or more months of history are needed to call a shift.</small>
                </div>
                <div
                  id="historical-shifts"
                  class="atlas-plot historical-shifts is-hidden"
                  aria-label="Cadence, question lenses, and wording signals by relative change from earlier to recent history"
                ></div>
                <p class="historical-shifts-scroll-hint" aria-hidden="true">
                  Scroll to see the change and before-to-after values &#8594;
                </p>
                <details class="chart-data">
                  <summary>Read what-changed data</summary>
                  <div id="historical-shifts-data" class="chart-data-list"></div>
                </details>
              </figure>
            </div>
          </section>

          <div class="workbench">
            <section id="topic-map" class="map-panel" aria-labelledby="topic-heading">
              <div class="section-heading">
                <div>
                  <p class="map-key">Things connected by meaning</p>
                  <h2 id="topic-heading">Topic map</h2>
                </div>
                <p>Node size is conversation count. Lines are semantic proximity.</p>
              </div>
              <form id="memory-search" class="memory-search" role="search">
                <label for="search-query">Search your mapped memory</label>
                <div class="search-field">
                  <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true">
                    <circle cx="10.5" cy="10.5" r="6.5"></circle>
                    <path d="m15.5 15.5 5 5"></path>
                  </svg>
                  <input
                    id="search-query"
                    name="query"
                    type="search"
                    autocomplete="off"
                    placeholder="Search what you asked, changed, or returned to"
                  />
                  <button type="submit">Search</button>
                </div>
                <div id="search-results" class="search-results" hidden></div>
              </form>
              <div id="graph-loading" class="graph-loading">
                <span></span>
                <strong>Semantic map is still forming.</strong>
                <small>Deterministic insights are ready below.</small>
              </div>
              <svg
                id="topic-graph"
                class="topic-graph is-hidden"
                viewBox="0 0 1000 620"
                role="group"
                aria-label="Interactive semantic topic graph"
              ></svg>
              <p class="mobile-graph-note">Focused neighborhood · the complete topic list follows.</p>
              <div id="topic-list" class="topic-list" aria-label="Accessible topic list"></div>
            </section>

            <div class="memory-sidecar">
              <section
                id="memory-chat"
                class="memory-chat-panel"
                aria-labelledby="memory-chat-heading"
              >
                <header>
                  <div>
                    <p class="map-key">Ask the graph</p>
                    <h2 id="memory-chat-heading">Memory Chat</h2>
                  </div>
                  <button id="unload-memory-chat" type="button" hidden>Unload model</button>
                </header>
                <p class="memory-chat-promise">
                  Your question traverses the map first. A small local model sees only the six
                  retrieved evidence stops—not the full ZIP.
                </p>

                <div id="memory-chat-gate" class="memory-chat-gate">
                  <dl>
                    <div><dt>Model</dt><dd>LaMini-Flan-T5 77M</dd></div>
                    <div><dt>Download</dt><dd>≈105 MB · cached by your browser</dd></div>
                    <div><dt>Boundary</dt><dd>Local q8 synthesis · English-focused</dd></div>
                  </dl>
                  <button id="enable-memory-chat" class="button-primary" type="button" disabled>
                    Available when the map is complete
                  </button>
                  <p id="memory-chat-model-status" role="status" aria-live="polite">
                    The chat model has not been loaded.
                  </p>
                  <progress id="memory-chat-model-progress" max="100" value="0" hidden></progress>
                </div>

                <div id="memory-chat-session" class="memory-chat-session" hidden>
                  <div
                    id="memory-chat-transcript"
                    class="memory-chat-transcript"
                    role="log"
                    aria-live="polite"
                    aria-label="Memory chat conversation"
                  >
                    <article class="memory-chat-message assistant">
                      <span>Local guide</span>
                      <p>Ask what you returned to, changed, rejected, or worked on over time.</p>
                    </article>
                  </div>

                  <section class="traversal-ledger" aria-labelledby="traversal-heading">
                    <div>
                      <p class="map-key">Visible retrieval route</p>
                      <h3 id="traversal-heading">How the graph answered</h3>
                    </div>
                    <ol id="memory-chat-route">
                      <li data-chat-stage="query"><i></i><span>Question received</span></li>
                      <li data-chat-stage="search"><i></i><span>Searching semantic memory</span></li>
                      <li data-chat-stage="topics"><i></i><span>Traversing topic routes</span></li>
                      <li data-chat-stage="evidence"><i></i><span>Building evidence pack</span></li>
                      <li data-chat-stage="answer"><i></i><span>Local synthesis</span></li>
                    </ol>
                    <div id="memory-chat-evidence" class="memory-chat-evidence"></div>
                  </section>

                  <form id="memory-chat-form">
                    <label for="memory-chat-query">Ask your mapped memory</label>
                    <textarea
                      id="memory-chat-query"
                      name="memory-question"
                      rows="3"
                      maxlength="600"
                      placeholder="What have I changed my mind about?"
                      required
                    ></textarea>
                    <button class="button-primary" type="submit">Traverse and answer</button>
                  </form>
                </div>

                <details class="memory-architecture-note">
                  <summary>Why this memory architecture is different</summary>
                  <p>
                    The retrieval route, sources, changed and refuted statements, confidence
                    controls, and local model boundary stay visible. Generated prose never becomes
                    a new memory automatically.
                  </p>
                  <p>
                    This is a product-behavior prototype, not a claim about current ChatGPT
                    internals. OpenAI’s own documentation says its legacy saved-memory experience
                    could become stale or contradictory.
                  </p>
                  <a
                    href="https://help.openai.com/en/articles/8590148-memory-faq"
                    target="_blank"
                    rel="noreferrer"
                  >Read OpenAI’s Memory FAQ ↗</a>
                </details>
              </section>

              <aside id="memory-ledger" class="ledger-panel" aria-labelledby="ledger-heading">
                <div class="section-heading compact">
                  <div>
                    <p class="map-key">Statement history</p>
                    <h2 id="ledger-heading">Memory ledger</h2>
                  </div>
                </div>
                <div id="ledger-tabs" class="ledger-tabs" role="tablist" aria-label="Fact states">
                  <button type="button" role="tab" data-status="current" aria-selected="true">
                    Current <span>0</span>
                  </button>
                  <button type="button" role="tab" data-status="updated" aria-selected="false">
                    Updated <span>0</span>
                  </button>
                  <button type="button" role="tab" data-status="refuted" aria-selected="false">
                    Refuted <span>0</span>
                  </button>
                  <button type="button" role="tab" data-status="contradicted" aria-selected="false">
                    Possible contradictions <span>0</span>
                  </button>
                </div>
                <div id="ledger-list" class="ledger-list">
                  <p class="empty-note">Fact candidates appear after semantic grouping.</p>
                </div>
                <p class="ledger-disclaimer">
                  Detected from explicit first-person wording. These are candidates, not verified
                  truths.
                </p>
              </aside>
            </div>
          </div>

          <section id="evolution" class="platform-section evolution-section" aria-labelledby="evolution-heading">
            <div class="section-heading">
              <div>
                <p class="map-key">Routes through time</p>
                <h2 id="evolution-heading">How your map changed</h2>
              </div>
              <p>Emerging, fading, and resurfacing are local trend labels—not explanations for why your interests changed.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="evolution-switcher" role="tablist" aria-label="Evolution evidence">
              <button type="button" role="tab" data-evolution="topics" aria-selected="true">Topics</button>
              <button type="button" role="tab" data-evolution="domains" aria-selected="false">Question domains</button>
              <button type="button" role="tab" data-evolution="language" aria-selected="false">Language signals</button>
            </div>
            <div class="evolution-grid">
              <div>
                <div id="evolution-list" class="evolution-list">
                  <p class="empty-note">Evolution routes appear after analysis.</p>
                </div>
              </div>
              <aside class="memory-change-board" aria-labelledby="memory-change-heading">
                <div class="lens-detail-heading">
                  <div>
                    <p class="map-key">Statements that moved</p>
                    <h3 id="memory-change-heading">Memory changes</h3>
                  </div>
                  <strong id="memory-change-total">0</strong>
                </div>
                <div id="memory-change-list" class="memory-change-list"></div>
              </aside>
            </div>
          </section>

          <section
            id="question-lenses"
            class="platform-section"
            aria-labelledby="lenses-heading"
          >
            <div class="section-heading">
              <div>
                <p class="map-key">Different ways to read the archive</p>
                <h2 id="lenses-heading">Question lenses</h2>
              </div>
              <p>
                Queries may appear in more than one domain. Open any result to inspect its
                supporting conversations.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div id="domain-lenses" class="domain-lenses"></div>
            <div class="lens-detail-grid">
              <article class="lens-detail-panel" aria-labelledby="typo-heading">
                <div class="lens-detail-heading">
                  <div>
                    <p class="map-key">Conservative writing signals</p>
                    <h3 id="typo-heading">Likely typos</h3>
                  </div>
                  <strong id="typo-total">0</strong>
                </div>
                <p id="typo-method"></p>
                <div id="typo-list" class="typo-list"></div>
              </article>
              <article class="lens-detail-panel" aria-labelledby="thread-heading">
                <div class="lens-detail-heading">
                  <div>
                    <p class="map-key">Conversations that changed tracks</p>
                    <h3 id="thread-heading">Conversation strands</h3>
                  </div>
                  <strong id="thread-total">0</strong>
                </div>
                <p id="thread-method"></p>
                <div id="thread-list" class="thread-list"></div>
              </article>
            </div>
          </section>

          <section
            id="repeated-questions"
            class="platform-section"
            aria-labelledby="repeats-heading"
          >
            <div class="section-heading">
              <div>
                <p class="map-key">Interchange patterns</p>
                <h2 id="repeats-heading">Questions you return to</h2>
              </div>
              <p>Exact wording and semantic repeats are kept distinct.</p>
            </div>
            <div id="repeat-summary" class="inline-summary"></div>
            <div id="repeat-list" class="repeat-list"></div>
          </section>

          <section
            id="reflection-questions"
            class="platform-section reflection-section"
            aria-labelledby="reflection-heading"
          >
            <div class="section-heading">
              <div>
                <p class="map-key">Prompts from your own evidence</p>
                <h2 id="reflection-heading">Questions your history asks you</h2>
