              <p>
                Invitations to review a repeat, correction, old memory, quiet theme, or wording
                spike—not conclusions about you.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div id="reflection-list" class="reflection-list"></div>
          </section>

          <section id="query-tone" class="platform-section" aria-labelledby="tone-heading">
            <div class="section-heading">
              <div>
                <p class="map-key">Wording, not personality</p>
                <h2 id="tone-heading">Query tone</h2>
              </div>
              <p id="tone-method"></p>
            </div>
            <div id="tone-bars" class="tone-bars"></div>
            <div class="emotion-heading">
              <p class="map-key">A more expressive vocabulary</p>
              <h3>Language signals in your queries</h3>
              <p id="emotion-method"></p>
            </div>
            <div id="emotion-bars" class="emotion-bars"></div>
          </section>

          <section
            id="efficiency"
            class="platform-section efficiency-section"
            aria-labelledby="efficiency-heading"
            hidden
          >
            <div class="section-heading">
              <div>
                <p class="map-key">What your sessions cost</p>
                <h2 id="efficiency-heading">Say less, do more</h2>
              </div>
              <p id="efficiency-method" class="method-note"></p>
            </div>

            <dl id="efficiency-stats" class="baseline-stats"></dl>

            <div class="efficiency-findings-heading">
              <p class="map-key">Issues, and what to do about them</p>
              <h3>Findings</h3>
            </div>
            <ol id="efficiency-findings" class="efficiency-findings"></ol>

            <div class="efficiency-grid">
              <div class="efficiency-panel">
                <p class="map-key">Cost per turn by session length</p>
                <h3>Why long sessions compound</h3>
                <p class="panel-note">
                  Every turn re-reads the session so far, so the same turn costs more the later it
                  happens.
                </p>
                <div id="efficiency-scaling" class="efficiency-bars"></div>
              </div>
              <div class="efficiency-panel">
                <p class="map-key">Where the spend concentrated</p>
                <h3>Your costliest sessions</h3>
                <p class="panel-note">
                  Ranked by context re-read. A very long thread is usually several tasks that never
                  got their own session.
                </p>
                <ul id="efficiency-costliest" class="efficiency-costliest"></ul>
              </div>
            </div>
          </section>

          <section id="rhythms" class="platform-section" aria-labelledby="rhythms-heading">
            <div class="section-heading">
              <div>
                <p class="map-key">Cadence over time</p>
                <h2 id="rhythms-heading">Rhythms</h2>
              </div>
              <p id="date-range"></p>
            </div>
            <div class="rhythm-toolbar">
              <div class="rhythm-measure" role="group" aria-labelledby="rhythm-measure-label">
                <span id="rhythm-measure-label">Measure</span>
                <button type="button" data-rhythm-measure="conversations" aria-pressed="true">
                  Conversations
                </button>
                <button type="button" data-rhythm-measure="words" aria-pressed="false">
                  Approx. words
                </button>
              </div>
              <label for="rhythm-route">
                <span>Question route</span>
                <select id="rhythm-route">
                  <option value="all">All conversations</option>
                  <option value="math">Math</option>
                  <option value="health">Health</option>
                  <option value="software">Software</option>
                  <option value="money">Money</option>
                  <option value="career">Career</option>
                  <option value="learning">Learning</option>
                  <option value="creative">Creative</option>
                  <option value="relationships">Relationships</option>
                  <option value="travel">Travel</option>
                  <option value="planning">Planning</option>
                </select>
              </label>
            </div>
            <div class="rhythm-summary" aria-live="polite">
              <div>
                <span>Selected total</span>
                <strong id="rhythm-total">—</strong>
              </div>
              <div>
                <span>Peak month</span>
                <strong id="rhythm-peak">—</strong>
              </div>
              <p id="rhythm-method">
                Monthly conversation starts across the selected period.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div
              id="activity-chart"
              class="activity-chart atlas-plot"
              aria-label="Monthly conversation activity"
            ></div>
            <details class="chart-data rhythm-data">
              <summary>Read rhythm data</summary>
              <div id="rhythm-data-list" class="chart-data-list"></div>
            </details>
          </section>

          <section class="methodology" aria-labelledby="method-heading">
            <p class="map-key">How the map was made</p>
            <h2 id="method-heading">Transparent by default.</h2>
            <div>
              <p>
                Statistics, question lenses, typo and thread-change candidates, query tone,
                language signals, and reflection prompts use local, inspectable rules. Topic
                relationships, semantic repeats, fact grouping, conversation strands, and search
                use normalized browser-loaded embeddings.
              </p>
              <p>
                Assistant assertions are excluded from the fact ledger. Large histories are
                sampled for semantic work while totals continue to cover the full parsed export.
                Confidence controls refilter stored candidates; they do not make inferred evidence
                certain.
              </p>
            </div>
          </section>
        </section>
      </main>
    </div>

